## Visualizing the Study Area

\*\*Code adapted from "CDFW 2020 Report Outer Coast Map.R" by A. Chang

**Loading Required Packages**

```{r}
library(ggplot2)
library(scales)
library(RColorBrewer)
library(ggmap)
library(sf)
library(sp)
library(cowplot)
library(ggrepel)
library(ggspatial)
```

**Loading Data**

```{r}
# Spatial Data
calesri<-read_sf(here("data","CA ESRI Coastline", "cazip.shp"))

# Study Site Data
sites<-read.csv(here("data", "sites.csv"))
```

**Converting Degrees Minutes Seconds to Decimal Degrees (DD)**

```{r}
# Formatting coordinates
chd = substr(sites$latitude, 3, 3)[1] #makes a circle
chm = substr(sites$latitude, 6, 6)[1] #makes a '
chs = substr(sites$latitude, 9, 9)[1] #makes a "

# Convertint Coordinates to DDD
sites$declatitude <- as.numeric(char2dms(sites$latitude, chd = chd, chm = chm, chs = chs)) 
sites$declongitude <- as.numeric(char2dms(sites$longitude, chd = chd, chm = chm, chs = chs))
```

**Creating Theme**

```{r}
map.theme <- theme_cowplot() +
